## 1. The §18 extractor defect is fixed and verified — with a plan consequence

`dump_wva_target_timeseries.py` now yields **54 snapshots / 54 hydrated** from the committed dwell
log, against 41 / **0** before. It **independently reproduces §18's headline** — per-replica
capacity 25,348 → 329,011, ratio **13.0×**, matching the 10–13× collapse §18 established by hand.
Recovered timeseries committed at `session-notes/scratch/wva_target_timeseries-20260808-dwell.json`.

**Planner action — one precondition needs rewording, and it is not mine to edit.**
The plan's §7.6.1 precondition "run `post_run_analyze.sh` **immediately**" is **necessary but not
sufficient**, and §18 already suspected this. Promptness defends against log *rotation*; it does
nothing against log-format *drift*, which is what actually broke the parse. The durable form is:

> **Save the raw controller log during the run (`kubectl logs ... > controller-<run-id>.log`), then
> parse. Re-parse offline with `--log-file <log> --no-window` if the window has passed.**

A saved log survives both failure modes; a fast parse survives only one. Suggest amending §7.6.1
accordingly. Related: part of the ladder run's missing `metrics/processed/wva_*` was attributed to
rotation and may in fact have been this drift.

## 2. Our own guide — new, and deliberately provisional

Dean's direction 2026-08-10: we have drifted enough from the upstream guide to warrant our own,
standing **alongside** it — *"we do not diverge from upstream. They have their docs. We just add
another guide."*

New: `docs/wva-benchmark-guide.md`. An edit I had made to the **shared**
`docs/developer-guide/two-variant-wva-benchmark.md` was **reverted**; my commits touch zero files
under `docs/developer-guide/`. Division of labor now explicit: **the new guide is the portable
procedure; `docs/two-variant-wva-pokprod-runbook.md` is one environment's operational detail.**

⚠️ **The guide is marked provisional in its own text: it has never been run from a clean clone.**
Dean's stated acceptance criterion — *"we would have to do a clean refresh test — start from a
clean WVA repo and see if following your guide builds everything correctly"* — is written into the
doc as a §10 checklist, framed so that every stumble is a **guide defect** rather than something to
work around in the shell. **This test is unperformed and needs a GPU cluster.** Nothing should
treat the guide as verified until it passes.

## 3. Image under test moved to the PR-2 anchor image — unverified against the parser

`WVA_IMAGE_TAG` now defaults to **`ta-0.9-anchor-pr2-20260809`** (was `ta-0.9`), per Dean
2026-08-10.

⚠️ **A tag change is a change of the code under test and can move the analyzer log format with
it** — exactly how the parse broke before. Two notes:

- The failure is now **loud** (warns, refuses to overwrite a good file, exits non-zero) rather than
  silent. That is a backstop, not a substitute for checking.
- Cheapest pre-check is a **read-only** look at the PR-2 branch's `engine_v2.go` log lines
  (`git -C ../ta-anchor-dynamic-refresh show ...`) before committing a run to it. **I have not done
  this**; happy to, on request. Otherwise: short run → confirm analysis fields populate → only then
  a long run.

Also relevant to the PR-2 thread: the extractor now records `scaleUpThreshold` /
`scaleDownBoundary` per tick, so a run on this image will **show** which thresholds are live rather
than leaving it inferred — directly useful given PR-2 changes where `k_sat` is sourced from.

